module gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.required_lane_green_over_a_population_it_never_offered

import std.types { NonEmptyStr }
import gunbc.recurring_failure_mode { RecurringFailureMode }

data required_lane_green_over_a_population_it_never_offered: RecurringFailureMode = RecurringFailureMode {
  identity: "required_lane_green_over_a_population_it_never_offered" as NonEmptyStr,

  receipts: [
    "**a required lane reports green while being silent by construction about a population it never offered to preparation** (INVALID STATE: a merge-blocking lane publishes a terminal verdict -- planned=N executed=N claims_failed=0 -- over a SELECTED subset, while declared claims outside that selection are neither planned nor executed nor reported as unattempted. A change lands with every required check green and breaks one of those claims; nothing in the gate can say so, because the broken claim was never a member of the set the gate adjudicated. HARM: the red persists on main indefinitely, and every subsequent green check re-attests to its absence. The failure is not that a witness went stale; it is that the instrument's denominator excluded it and the verdict did not say so at the grain a reader consumes.) ",

    "THE POPULATION IS NOT HIDDEN, WHICH IS WHY THIS OUTLASTS ANY SINGLE FIX. The required floor lane PRINTS it, under `outside this run's universe, kept as record and NOT counted as debt (declared, but preparation never offered them -- gate closure or discovery exclusion)`. The defect is that a green required check is what a reader consumes, and the exclusion list lives in a log nobody opens when the check is green. An accurate report at one grain and a misleading answer at the grain of the decision are compatible states. ",

    "MEASURED INSTANCE, dated and joined at identity. `test.claim.fleet_converge_plan_witness.ci_runner_grants_derive_from_the_closed_vocabulary` asserted `length(grants) == 6`. `ci_runner_sudo_binaries` grew to seven members when `SudoUseradd` landed in 4b7371d1f64 (#10357, 2026-09-04) with all required lanes green. The witness went red that day and was still red on 2026-09-05, discovered only because an unrelated lane read the floor log rather than the check mark, and only because that lane had edited a production module whose witnesses sit in the same excluded set. A SECOND claim in the same population was red on both sides of that lane's diff and traces to THE SAME COMMIT: `witness_scope_row_is_what_separates_the_two_baselines` asserts that the scope row is the only line separating two baseline texts, and 4b7371d1f64 also added `runner_unit_standings_baseline_rows` to the full-host arm, which answers `units:unobserved` for unobserved standings -- a non-scope row present in one text and absent from the other. So ONE all-green pull request broke TWO witnesses in the excluded population on the same day. Which of the witness or the model is wrong there is a design question for its owning lane and is deliberately not decided here. ",

    "THE EXCLUDED SET IS NOT A ROUNDING ERROR: roughly 80 claim identities on run 33945448419, spanning `test.claim.host_axis_caps.*`, `test.claim.fleet_converge_plan_witness.*`, `test.claim.live_deploy.readiness.*`, `test.claim.roadmap_static_site_witness.*` and others. Those modules are imported by production modules that ordinary changes DO touch, so the excluded set is not a quarantine of dead code; it is reachable subject matter with no reporting path. ",

    "DISTINGUISHING WITNESS, and the shape that made it decisive rather than merely suspicious: run the excluded claims at BASE and at HEAD and compare the failing SETS BY IDENTITY, never a conjunction's single bit. One generated function over the whole roster, mapping each witness to the empty string when it holds and to its own name prefixed FAIL: when it does not, and joining the results, names every failure in ONE run per side. Identical sets prove a change contributed nothing; a difference IS the contribution. A conjunction can only report that at least one member was already red, which does not separate pre-existing from introduced -- that distinction is the whole attribution question. ",

    "RECOGNITION RULE, phrased to fire before the green is trusted: ask WHAT THE DENOMINATOR WAS, not whether the verdict was green. `claims_failed=0` is a statement about `planned`, and `planned` is a selection. Before crediting a required lane for a module you changed, check whether that module's witnesses are members of the run's universe -- and treat `not offered to preparation` as UNMEASURED, never as passed. The tell is a lane whose totals reconcile perfectly (planned == executed == terminal, failed 0) beside a separately printed exclusion list nobody joined against the change. ",

    "BOUNDARY AGAINST selection_view_read_as_population, WHICH IS ADJACENT AND NOT THE SAME: there a reader mistakes a filtered VIEW for the whole population while reading the instrument directly. Here the instrument is correct and complete about its own universe, publishes its exclusions honestly, and the misreading happens at a DIFFERENT ARTIFACT -- the merge-blocking check state -- which carries no denominator at all. Fixing the reader's grep does not help; the check is what gates, and the check cannot express `green over a subset`. ",

    "THE ROW NAMES TWO MECHANISMS THAT COMPOUND, AND ONLY THE SECOND IS A NEW CLASS. What BROKE was an oracle defect -- a merge-blocking witness comparing a live population to a numeric literal -- and that rule is already normative in DESIGN section 5, which admits such a literal only when it is grounded in a controlled fixture, an external or versioned authority, an explicit policy budget, or a monotone debt contract over a closed subject universe. No second identity is minted for it here: the design document is its authority and a ledger row would be a fork of that. What is NEW, and what this identity carries, is why nobody could KNOW for a day -- the lane reported green while the broken witness was not in the set it adjudicated. The two have different ceilings and different triggers, and a reader given only the first would file this as an anecdote about one stale witness. ",

    "POPULATION OF THE ORACLE SHAPE, STATED AS CANDIDATES AND NOT AS DEFECTS, AND DELIBERATELY WITHOUT A COUNT. The shape recurs well beyond the one site this row proves, and the population is named by its PRODUCER rather than transcribed: run `git grep -nE` over `dag/test` and `src/v2/test` for the pattern `length[(]xs: [a-z_]+[(][)]?[^)]*[)] == [0-9]+`, written with bracket expressions so it carries no backslash escape. No total is recorded here on purpose. A copied total is unreachable from the query that owns it and rots without anyone touching either end, which is DESIGN section 6, and a row whose whole subject is a literal that went stale beside the population it described is the last place that may carry one. An unknown subset of the matches is legitimately grounded under section 5 carve-outs: some are invariants comparing to zero, some are controlled fixtures, and the self-host frontier counts are the monotone-debt case IF their contract is declared. NONE has been adjudicated except the one this row proves, which was ungrounded and had been red for a day. So the query returns CANDIDATES; it does not return a defect count, and no number derived from it may be quoted as one. ",

    "BOUNDARY AGAINST ceiling_never_exercised_for_a_population_the_census_cannot_plan, WHICH SHARES THIS POPULATION AND IS A DIFFERENT DEFECT: there a COST BOUND is never evaluated for identities the ordinary floor never plans, so the first edit that makes one run discovers the line as a surprise merge block. Here the VERDICT is the thing never taken -- the claim's own pass or fail -- and the surprise is that there is none, indefinitely. Same excluded set, different unmeasured quantity: one is a bound that has never been applied, the other is a truth value that is never reported. A repair to either leaves the other exactly as it was. ",

    "BOUNDARY AGAINST green_reported_over_a_population_the_instrument_does_not_own, WHICH IS THE NEAREST ROW IN THE LEDGER AND MUST BE READ BEFORE THIS ONE. Its thesis is nearly this sentence, so the two would nickname one concept if the mechanisms were the same. They are not, and the difference is WHERE THE UNCOVERED HALF LIVES. There, TWO ACTUATORS split one population -- claim_executor --required-regen and generated_artifact_gate main_wet -- and the one lanes habitually run denominates only its own half; the other half IS owned, by the other actuator, and coverage for it EXISTS UNRUN. The repair is the split: join the two denominators, or run both. Here ONE lane owns its whole declared population, selects a subset of it, and publishes a verdict that does not disclose the selection; the excluded claims are offered by NO actuator, so coverage for them exists NOWHERE. ",

    "THE TRIGGERS ARE THEREFORE DISJOINT, WHICH IS THE TEST THAT SETTLES IT RATHER THAN THE PROSE. Joining the two generated-artifact actuators leaves every one of the excluded claims exactly as dark, because neither actuator ever offered them. Making a lane adjudicate its own denominator says nothing about a second actuator owning a different population, so it leaves that row untouched. A repair to either is invisible to the other, which is what a genuinely distinct class looks like -- and had the test come out the other way, the honest outcome was to fold these receipts into that row rather than mint this identity. ",

    "NEIGHBOURS CHECKED BY IDENTITY RATHER THAN BY MEMORY, over all rows in gunbc.recurring_failure_mode.roster. Three are adjacent and bounded: selection_view_read_as_population (the misreading happens at the instrument, not at a downstream check carrying no denominator), ceiling_never_exercised_for_a_population_the_census_cannot_plan (a bound never applied, not a truth value never reported), and green_reported_over_a_population_the_instrument_does_not_own (above). Two rows landed on the roster the same day this one did, and both were re-checked at identity grain rather than assumed distinct: roster_is_its_own_denominator is a hand-authored list standing in for a subject definition, so the missing rows are UNSTATED -- here the excluded identities ARE stated, printed by the run itself, and the defect is that nothing joins them against the change; and instrument_answers_outside_its_domain reports a false FINDING when asked outside its range, the opposite direction of harm from a false GREEN, which is why its repair -- a typed out-of-domain relation at the query -- does not discharge this class, whose instrument answered correctly about the universe it was given. A third row landed on the roster while this one was in review and was checked the same way: discriminating_evidence_authored_into_the_operational_population is a check whose expecting-red probe LIVES IN the population it testifies about, so the instrument is wrong about a subject it did measure. Here the instrument is right about every subject it measured and the excluded identities were never subjects at all -- contaminated denominator versus truncated one, and moving the evidence to a fixture, which discharges that class, leaves this one untouched. The nearest row on the roster today is preparation_membership_derived_from_the_execution_selector, and the two are one selection mechanism cutting two different populations: there the unprepared subject is a PRODUCTION MODULE that is never compiled, so the ordinary floor -- names resolve, variants eliminate -- goes unchecked over code no selected test imports; here the unoffered subject is a CLAIM that is compiled and enrolled but whose own pass or fail is never taken. Deriving preparation from the roster would discharge that row and leave this one exactly as it is, because a claim can be prepared and still never adjudicated. One more is worth naming and is NOT this class: required_evidence_absent_reads_as_evidence_of_pass is a gate admitting because NOTHING has reported, keying on observed failure where it needed observed success. Here everything reported, the verdict is real and correct about its universe, and the defect is that the universe was a selection nobody joined against the change. ",

    "RUNG FOUND AT: mitigatable -- the exclusion is printed and can be read by a diligent author, which is review diligence rather than a mechanism. ",

    "CEILING: STRUCTURALLY IMPOSSIBLE, corrected from an earlier reading of this row and the correction recorded rather than silently swapped, because the mistake is the instructive part. The first form capped the class at mechanically preventable and argued: a claim may be excluded for legitimate cost or discovery reasons, therefore exclusion cannot be made impossible, therefore the ceiling is a gate. That CONFLATES EXCLUSION WITH SILENCE ABOUT EXCLUSION. Exclusion is legitimate and stays legitimate; the invalid state is a terminal verdict that does not say which declared identities it declined to offer. That state has a constructor today only because the verdict is built from the offered subset alone. ",

    "WHAT MAKES IT REACHABLE, and it is exactly what section 4b asks of a decidable and fully modeled class: the declared claim universe and the run offered set are both already DERIVED, so their difference is decidable, and a terminal verdict can be constructed FROM A TOTAL DISPOSITION over the declared universe rather than from the offered subset -- every declared identity carrying either an executed outcome or a typed NotOffered reason, with no catch-all arm. Under that carrier a verdict silent about an excluded identity is not caught, it is UNWRITABLE: the excluded arm has to be constructed, with its reason, before any verdict exists at all. Nothing there requires forbidding exclusion, which is why the legitimacy of exclusion never was the limitation. ",

    "NEXT-RUNG TRIGGER, STATED AS A CAPABILITY: the run terminal verdict is DERIVED AS A TOTAL PROJECTION from the declared claim identity universe, so a verdict that omits an identity has no constructor. The refusal form -- the lane joins a change reachable claim identities against its offered universe and REFUSES, typed and located, when the blast radius contains a claim it did not offer -- remains the legitimate RUNG 2 step on the way there, and it must not be reported as the ceiling reached, because both the roster and the offered set stay separately writable under it and a single author can drop an identity from both in one change. Enumerating todays exclusions, or repairing the two claims found red, satisfies neither rung and leaves the next excluded claim exactly as dark. ",
  ],

  evidence: [],
}
